WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:08.124
This is GitCat: a cozy, open-source Git client, built so that anything you do can be taken back.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.669
Here's CPython, with over a hundred and thirty thousand commits.

00:00:14.669 --> 00:00:21.500
The graph is laid out in Rust and drawn on a virtualized canvas, so it stays smooth all the way down.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:33.382
Select any commit for the full story: author and committer side by side, and a signature that Git itself has verified.

00:00:34.558 --> 00:00:41.182
Diffs are syntax-highlighted, and you can pop one out into its own window, to read it next to your work.

00:00:48.826 --> 00:00:54.778
Everything is one Control-K away: commits, branches, and every action.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:01.185
Now, something dangerous: a hard reset that throws away the last few commits.

00:01:01.185 --> 00:01:05.760
Tama warns you first, and pins a snapshot before anything moves.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:12.742
Changed your mind?

00:01:12.742 --> 00:01:14.157
Press Control-Z.

00:01:14.157 --> 00:01:18.579
Every change is snapshotted, so Undo always works.

00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:20.702
Even Undo can be undone.

00:01:22.058 --> 00:01:22.741
GitCat.

00:01:22.741 --> 00:01:24.886
Git you can take back.

00:01:24.886 --> 00:01:28.298
Free for macOS, Windows, and Linux.

